---
layout: layouts/base.njk
description: Data modeling, reconciliation, data quality and structured evaluation — and a journal about the systems that carry them.
---
{% from "partials/figure.njk" import figure %}

{# ===================================================================
   Cover. The name is the one dark object in the room. Motion 1 of 3
   wipes it up from below, once, on load. See DESIGN.md.
   =================================================================== #}
<div class="shell">
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="name-h">
    <p class="eyebrow">{{ site.author.role }}</p>
    <h1 class="hero__name" id="name-h">{{ site.title }}</h1>
    <p class="lead">Notes on data, evidence, and the strange act of
      deciding whether a number can be trusted.</p>
    <div class="hero__links">
      <a href="mailto:{{ site.author.email }}">{{ site.author.email }}</a>
      <span class="needs-content">[NEEDS CONTENT: résumé PDF. Held until the
        Q1–Q5 conflicts resolve. Highest-priority gap on the site.]</span>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

{# Ticker. One marquee on the whole site, and it stops dead under
   prefers-reduced-motion rather than merely slowing down. #}
<div class="ticker" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="ticker__track">
    <span>Reconciliation</span><span>·</span><span>Data dictionaries</span><span>·</span>
    <span>Structured evaluation</span><span>·</span><span>Entity resolution</span><span>·</span>
    <span>Validation rules</span><span>·</span><span>Field notes</span><span>·</span>
    <span>Reconciliation</span><span>·</span><span>Data dictionaries</span><span>·</span>
    <span>Structured evaluation</span><span>·</span><span>Entity resolution</span><span>·</span>
    <span>Validation rules</span><span>·</span><span>Field notes</span><span>·</span>
  </div>
</div>

{# ===================================================================
   What I do. The one sand-filled section. Label colour steps up to
   --secondary inside it: --muted is 4.03:1 on sand and fails.
   =================================================================== #}
<div class="panel">
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="section" id="approach" aria-labelledby="approach-h">
      <h2 class="section__head" id="approach-h">What I do</h2>
      <p class="lead">Most of my work is making two systems agree on what a
        record means.</p>
      <p>Data models and dictionaries that hold up when someone else uses
        them, reconciliation between systems that were never built to match,
        validation rules that catch the records worth a second look, and
        evaluation work scored against written criteria rather than
        impressions. Currently a master&rsquo;s candidate in data analytics
        engineering at Northeastern, looking for full-time analytics roles.</p>

      <ul class="rail">
        <li><span class="rail__figure">1,080</span><span class="rail__label">records routed to human review</span></li>
        <li><span class="rail__figure">1,194</span><span class="rail__label">federal passages structured</span></li>
        <li><span class="rail__figure">203</span><span class="rail__label">fields in a data dictionary</span></li>
        <li><span class="rail__figure">3,000+</span><span class="rail__label">participants in a program reported on</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>

{# =================================================================== #}
<div class="shell">

  {%- set posts = collections.writing %}
  {%- set featured = (posts | where("featured", true) | limit(1))[0] or posts[0] %}

  {%- if featured %}
  <section class="section" id="featured" aria-labelledby="featured-h">
    <h2 class="eyebrow" id="featured-h">The feature</h2>
    <div class="feature">
      <a class="feature__media" href="{{ featured.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
        {{ figure(featured.data.coverImage, featured.data.coverAlt or featured.data.title,
                  featured.data.coverCaption, featured.data.coverCredit, none, "4/3") }}
      </a>
      <div class="feature__body">
        <p class="labelrow">
          <span class="labelrow__cat">{{ featured.data.category }}</span>
          <span class="labelrow__sep" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <time datetime="{{ featured.data.date | iso }}">{{ featured.data.date | readable }}</time>
          <span class="labelrow__sep" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span>{{ featured.templateContent | readingTime }} min read</span>
        </p>
        <h3 class="feature__title"><a href="{{ featured.url }}">{{ featured.data.title }}</a></h3>
        <p>{{ featured.data.description }}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endif %}

  {# Editorial index, numbered. Not cards. #}
  <section class="section" id="contents" aria-labelledby="contents-h">
    <h2 class="section__head" id="contents-h">Contents</h2>
    <ol class="index index--lg">
      {%- for item in posts | limit(6) %}
      <li class="index__row">
        <span class="index__num">{{ loop.index | pad }}</span>
        <span class="index__main">
          <a class="index__link" href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a>
          <span class="index__desc">{{ item.data.description }}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="index__meta">
          <span class="index__cat">{{ item.data.category }}</span>
          <time datetime="{{ item.data.date | iso }}">{{ item.data.date | readable }}</time>
        </span>
      </li>
      {%- else %}
      <li class="empty">No writing published yet.</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
    <p class="more"><a href="/writing/">All writing</a></p>
  </section>
</div>

{# Visual break: a generative SVG artifact, drawn in code. No stock imagery. #}
<div class="shell">
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="plate-h">
    <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="plate-h">Plate</h2>
    <figure class="plate" data-reveal>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1200 320" role="img" aria-label="Abstract chart: a scatter of records, most resolved automatically, a band routed to human review." preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
        <g class="plate__grid">
          {%- for i in range(0, 13) %}
          <line x1="{{ i * 100 }}" y1="0" x2="{{ i * 100 }}" y2="320"></line>
          {%- endfor %}
          {%- for i in range(0, 5) %}
          <line x1="0" y1="{{ i * 80 }}" x2="1200" y2="{{ i * 80 }}"></line>
          {%- endfor %}
        </g>
        {# Two populations, deliberately separated, so the picture argues
           something instead of being texture: a dense mass the rule resolved,
           and a thin accent band it refused to decide. #}
        <g class="plate__dots">
          {%- for i in range(0, 260) %}
          {%- set x = (i * 173) % 1186 + 7 %}
          {%- set y = 140 + ((i * i * 17) % 170) %}
          <circle cx="{{ x }}" cy="{{ y }}" r="2"></circle>
          {%- endfor %}
        </g>
        <g class="plate__dots plate__dots--review">
          {%- for i in range(0, 34) %}
          {%- set x = (i * 349) % 1150 + 25 %}
          {%- set y = 22 + ((i * 53) % 78) %}
          <circle cx="{{ x }}" cy="{{ y }}" r="4" class="is-review"></circle>
          {%- endfor %}
        </g>
        <line class="plate__cut" x1="0" y1="126" x2="1200" y2="126"></line>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="fig__caption">Below the rule: matches the criteria resolved. Above it: the records that went to a person.</span>
        <span class="fig__meta">Drawn in SVG · deterministic · no data source</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
</div>

<div class="shell">
  {# Selected project. #}
  {%- set proj = collections.projects %}
  {# Explicitly featured, not most recent. Sorting by date put an unstarted
     TKTK shell on the front page ahead of the one finished study. #}
  {%- set p = (proj | where("featured", true) | limit(1))[0] or proj[0] %}
  {%- if p %}
  <section class="section" id="selected" aria-labelledby="selected-h">
    <h2 class="section__head" id="selected-h">Selected project</h2>
    <article class="entry">
      <h3 class="entry__title"><a href="{{ p.url }}">{{ p.data.title }}</a></h3>
      <p class="entry__meta">{{ p.data.period }}{% if p.data.tools %}. {{ p.data.tools | join(", ") }}.{% endif %}</p>
      <div class="entry__body"><p>{{ p.data.description }}</p></div>
      {%- if p.data.figures %}
      <ul class="entry__figures">
        {%- for f in p.data.figures | limit(3) %}
        <li><span class="rail__figure">{{ f.value }}</span><span class="rail__label">{{ f.label }}</span></li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
      {%- endif %}
    </article>
    <p class="more"><a href="/projects/">All projects</a></p>
  </section>
  {%- endif %}

  {# Now. #}
  <section class="section" id="now" aria-labelledby="now-h">
    <h2 class="section__head" id="now-h">Now</h2>
    <dl class="catalog">
      <div class="catalog__row">
        <dt>Studying</dt>
        <dd>M.S. Data Analytics Engineering, Northeastern. 2026&ndash;2027.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="catalog__row">
        <dt>Building</dt>
        <dd><span class="needs-content">[NEEDS CONTENT: what she is actually
          building right now. This module is only worth having if it is kept
          current; a stale Now section is worse than none.]</span></dd>
      </div>
      <div class="catalog__row">
        <dt>Reading</dt>
        <dd><span class="needs-content">[NEEDS CONTENT: current reading. See
          /library/ for the full list.]</span></dd>
      </div>
      <div class="catalog__row">
        <dt>Looking for</dt>
        <dd>Full-time analytics roles.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  {# Field images. #}
  <section class="section" id="field-images" aria-labelledby="fi-h">
    <h2 class="section__head" id="fi-h">Field images</h2>
    <div class="scraps">
      {%- for i in range(0, 4) %}
      <figure class="scrap scrap--{{ i + 1 }}" data-reveal>
        <div class="fig__placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 1/1">
          <span class="needs-content">[NEEDS CONTENT: field image {{ i + 1 }}]</span>
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          <span class="fig__caption">TKTK</span>
          <span class="fig__meta">TKTK · TKTK</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="more"><a href="/about/">About her</a></p>
  </section>

  {# Reading list callout, set in the page rather than floated over it. #}
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="sub-h">
    <div class="callout callout--wide">
      <h2 class="eyebrow" id="sub-h">The feed</h2>
      <p>New field notes are published here and to a plain Atom feed. No
        email list, no popup, nothing to unsubscribe from.</p>
      <p class="more"><a href="/feed.xml">Subscribe via Atom</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
